# AI Gateway rules

- All provider access goes through `AiGateway -> AiProvider -> provider adapter`.
- Frontend uses internal Vimla model IDs, never arbitrary provider model strings.
- Model availability/capabilities/prices are curated/versioned server data.
- Provider requests only start after successful usage reservation and security/rate/concurrency checks.
- Server controls context, output-token cap, per-request cost cap and safety margin.
- Browser cannot supply provider price, raw history/system prompt, provider model ID or max token value unless explicitly reviewed.
- Record full provider actual cost separately from user-settled usage.
- Missing/ambiguous provider usage must not become a free request; use reconciliation/anomaly states.
- Avoid unsafe automatic retries for potentially billable requests.
- Client disconnect after provider start is not proof of zero cost.
- AI output is untrusted content and must be rendered safely.
- Normal tests use mock providers/transports; CI must not spend real provider money.
